Rhiza OS Template
version: 2026.09-v5
released: 2026-09-30

What changed in this version, in plain words:

- A launch library: launch-facts, launch-calendar, messaging, jv-kit,
  curriculum, leads, registrations, follow-up. One page of facts per
  launch, and everything else is built from it.
- Onboarding ends by offering help with something real: a launch you're
  in the middle of, a new one, or getting organized.
- Your email list's groups have one home, in knowledge/core/audience.md,
  asked the first time a launch needs them.
- A leads folder that points you to your own tool once it's connected.
- Leaner: the audit and checkup skills are gone. Pickup now notices if
  the hourly backup has stopped.

Previous version: 2026.09-v4 (2026-09-22): hourly backup, knowledge/core/,
pickup and write-like-me, the handoff close, the quality bar, the voice
bank.

Your OS records this version number in decisions.md when it installs, so
you can always tell which template you started from.
